<IndustryPage {...pageData}>
<p>UK logistics and haulage firms operate on tight margins in a highly competitive market. Rising fuel costs, driver shortages, and customer demands for real-time visibility all add pressure. Bespoke software can help you optimise routes, manage fleets, and deliver the tracking experience customers now expect - but most operators are still running on a combination of legacy transport management systems, paper proof-of-delivery sheets, and spreadsheet-based planning that can't keep up with real-world complexity.</p>
<p>Off-the-shelf transport management software was designed for large enterprises and priced accordingly. It handles basic routing but can't account for your specific constraints - driver hours and working time directive compliance, vehicle height and weight restrictions on particular routes, customer-specific delivery windows, or backloading opportunities across your network. Generic fleet management tools track vehicles but don't connect to your job costing or invoicing systems, so finance teams still rekey delivery data. Warehouse management systems built for e-commerce don't understand cross-dock operations or groupage handling.</p>
<p>We build custom software for UK logistics firms - from transport management systems and route optimisation to warehouse management and driver apps. We understand logistics operations, from the warehouse to the delivery point, and we build systems that integrate with your existing infrastructure. Whether it's a bespoke TMS that plans routes around your specific constraints, a driver mobile app that captures electronic proof of delivery and updates customers in real time, or a warehouse management system that handles your particular goods-in and cross-dock workflows, bespoke software fits the way your operation actually runs.</p>
<p>Logistics compliance is unforgiving. Driver hours under the Working Time Directive, vehicle roadworthiness under O-licence obligations, and ADR requirements for hazardous goods all demand precise record-keeping. Bespoke software can automate tachograph data analysis, flag potential hours violations before they occur, and maintain digital maintenance records that satisfy DVSA inspections - replacing paper-based systems that are easily lost and impossible to audit quickly.</p>
<p>A UK regional haulier operating 40 vehicles was losing an estimated £50,000 annually to empty running and inefficient routing. Their off-the-shelf TMS couldn't optimise for backloading opportunities or customer-specific time windows. We built a bespoke route optimisation tool that identified backloading matches across their customer base and planned routes around delivery constraints. Empty running dropped by 18% within six months, fuel costs fell proportionally, and the planning team reduced from three full-time staff to two.</p>
<p>Logistics is a sector where bespoke software delivers clear ROI. Every mile, every job, and every delivery generates data. The opportunity is building software that turns that data into optimised routes, automated workflows, and real-time visibility across your operation.</p>

